# Try the auth API by hand. VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client),
# start the server (`dotnet run` in server/), then click "Send Request" above each block.
# Cookies are remembered between requests, like a browser.

@base = http://localhost:5137/api/auth
@username = alice
@password = my-long-passphrase

### Who am I? (401 until you sign up or log in)
GET {{base}}/me

### Sign up: the response shows your recovery code ONCE
# @name signup
POST {{base}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{username}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Log out
POST {{base}}/logout

### Log in
POST {{base}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{username}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Forgot password: reset with the recovery code (gives you a NEW code; the old one stops working)
# Paste your code over the {{...}} below if you signed up in an earlier session.
POST {{base}}/recover
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{username}}", "recoveryCode": "{{signup.response.body.$.recoveryCode}}", "newPassword": "another-long-passphrase" }

### Things that should fail: a common password
POST {{base}}/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "bob", "password": "password123" }
